      "content": "Right, emphasis is key. But I'm looking at the actual p-value for the Protein-X correlation right now and it's sitting at 0.06. I'm a bit worried that the reviewers are going to jump all over that since it's technically above the 0.05 threshold. How do we handle that in the text? I don't want to be dishonest, but I also can't afford to have them dismiss the whole study because of one marginal p-value.",
